---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/11-04/', manual='https://doriclenses.com/downloads/UserManual/UserManual_NC500_V1.0.0.pdf', consolePhoto='https://neuro.doriclenses.com/cdn/shop/files/DNC500.webp?v=1769698006&width=1225', cubePhoto='https://doriclenses.com/downloads/Website/FMC4-GCaMP_BuiltInLED%28with%20driver%29AndDetector.webp', drawing='https://www.doriclenses.com/downloads/drawings/Drawing_iLFMC4-G3-GCaMP.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Doric NC500 and Mini Cube Gen. 3 · capped exteriors" description="Orbit the capped, disconnected documentary exteriors and compare fixed orientations of an unrelated coordinate graphic." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment dc"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/11-04/">← Equipment 11-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#dc-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">11-04 · DORMANT EXTERIORS & DETACHED DRAWING / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Doric NC500 and Mini Cube Gen. 3</h2><p>Orbit the capped, disconnected Doric exteriors. On the separate display, rotate a fixed coordinate card by a quarter turn. Its signed vector changes, while the distance between the same two points stays the same.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Documentary components and independent display</h3><div id="dc-view" aria-label="Orbitable inactive console, capped mini cube with externally visible fins, and physically separate card display"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-dc-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-dc-view="console">Console face</button><button data-dc-view="cube">Mini cube exterior</button><button data-dc-view="display">Detached display</button><button id="dc-cycle">Next card orientation</button></div>
<p id="dc-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. All hardware remains fixed and disconnected. The teal badge belongs to the display only.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached coordinate card</h3><canvas id="dc-plot" width="660" height="450" aria-label="Unaffiliated drafting coordinate card with points A, B, C and a line between A and B"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Card view<select id="dc-case"><option value="original">Original orientation</option><option value="ccw">Quarter-turn counterclockwise</option><option value="cw">Quarter-turn clockwise</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="dc-inspect">Inspect vector and length</button><button id="dc-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="dc-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a fixed orientation and inspect line A–B.</p><output id="dc-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="dc-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="dc-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected documentary components: Doric Neuroscience Console 500 (NC500) and the four-port integrated Mini Cube Gen. 3 (iLFMC4-G3). <a href={manual+'#page=8'}>NC500 manual v1.0.0, p. 8</a> identifies the dimensions; the <a href={consolePhoto}>Doric console product photograph</a> establishes three groups of exterior connector silhouettes. The <a href={cubePhoto}>Doric mini cube product image</a> and <a href={drawing+'#page=1'}>outer envelope drawing B340-1330-001 (2022)</a> establish body, tab and rear-fin geometry. Radii, cap shapes and cosmetic features are visually inferred. No original diagram or photograph is reproduced; caps are original blind stand-ins, and markings are intentionally left unreadable.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original render of the dark long Doric console and separate mini cube with unconnected caps"/><figcaption>Original front comparison. Neither device is connected; the display is a fictional third object.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original closer rendering of the dark front faces and mini cube with externally visible fins"/><figcaption>Original comparison render based on the product photographs. Capped protrusions and blank screens are deliberately nonfunctional.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>NC500 external envelope</td><td>400 W × 115 D × 50 H mm</td><td>Metric GLB bounds match the nominal manual size, including model caps.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mini cube outer envelope</td><td>147 W × 109 D × 58 H mm</td><td>Metric maximum spans include mounting tabs and visible outer details. 107 × 68 × 52 mm body modeled separately.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Detached vector A→B</td><td>(18,9) → (−9,18) or (9,−18) mm</td><td>Each card view preserves √405 = 20.124612 mm. Source positions and IDs do not change.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original register acceptance</td><td>Combined fluorescence and background calculation</td><td>Not implemented or run. This build has no biological, optical, stimulation, acquisition or instrument operation.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>A counterclockwise quarter turn switches (x,y) to (−y,x); clockwise switches to (y,−x). The display draws the same three immutable authored positions in either orientation; an inspection computes the A-to-B difference and Euclidean magnitude. The JSON report includes the unaffected source positions, displayed coordinates, version, and millimeter units. It ships no specimen, experiment data, optical path, parameter, protocol or workstation handoff.</p>
<p><a href={base+'doric-nc500-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'coordinates-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/11-04/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.dc{max-width:76rem}.dc .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.dc section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.dc .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.dc .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.dc label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.dc input,.dc select,.dc button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.dc button{cursor:pointer}.dc button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.dc .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.dc #dc-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.dc #dc-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.dc #dc-plot,.dc img{width:100%;height:auto}.dc #dc-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.dc #dc-status.error{color:#a54a34}.dc .scroll{overflow:auto}.dc table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.dc td,.dc th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.dc figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.dc .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
